    "body": "## Description\r\n This PR expands and standardizes the agent skill system for Visdom.\r\n \r\n ### What was added\r\n - Added multiple new skills for common workflows:\r\n   - `auth-login`\r\n   - `callback-events`\r\n   - `ci-workflow-debug`\r\n   - `docs-sync`\r\n   - `env-persistence`\r\n   - `environment-views`\r\n   - `frontend-pane-lifecycle`\r\n   - `handler-auth-flow`\r\n   - `offline-replay`\r\n   - `performance-streaming`\r\n   - `polling-parity`\r\n   - `python-client-api`\r\n   - `update-patching`\r\n - Added AI instruction entry files pointing to single source of truth (`AGENTS.md`):\r\n   - `CLAUDE.md`\r\n   - `CODEX.md`\r\n   - `GEMINI.md`\r\n   - `.github/copilot-instructions.md`\r\n \r\n ### What was changed\r\n - Standardized all skills with a consistent scaffold:\r\n   - `SKILL.md` with clear sections (`When to Use`, `Core Workflow`, `Guardrails`, `Documentation`, \r\n`Assets`, `Tests`)\r\n - Added `_defaults/` templates and propagated them across skill directories.\r\n - Updated `.agents/skills/README.md` with the new directory structure and complete skill index.\r\n \r\n ## Motivation and Context\r\n The skill ecosystem was inconsistent across folders and lacked a shared format for \r\nreferences/assets/testing guidance.\r\n This PR creates a clean, repeatable structure so future skills are easier to author, review, and use \r\nreliably across AI assistants.\r\n \r\n ## How Has This Been Tested?\r\n - Validated skill frontmatter format and naming constraints (`name` matches folder, valid slug format, \r\nrequired fields present).\r\n - Verified scaffold files exist for every skill:\r\n   - `references/REFERENCE.md`\r\n   - `references/TESTS.md`\r\n   - `assets/README.md`\r\n - Confirmed no references to `VISDOM_USER_GUIDE.md` or `VISDOM_INTERNALS.md` remain in skill files.\r\n \r\n No runtime product code paths were changed in this PR (docs/skill/instruction structure only).\r\n \r\n ## Screenshots (if appropriate):\r\n N/A\r\n \r\n ## Types of changes\r\n - [ ] Bug fix (non-breaking change which fixes an issue)\r\n - [x] New feature (non-breaking change which adds functionality)\r\n - [ ] Breaking change (fix or feature that would cause existing functionality to not work as expected)\r\n - [x] Code refactor or cleanup (changes to existing code for improved readability or performance)\r\n \r\n ## Checklist:\r\n - [ ] I adapted the version number under `py/visdom/VERSION` according to [Semantic \r\nVersioning](https://semver.org/)\r\n - [x] My code follows the code style of this project.\r\n - [x] My change requires a change to the documentation.\r\n - [x] I have updated the documentation accordingly.\r\n",
